    <string name="settings_render_mode">Rendering</string>
    <string name="settings_server_render_note">Server rendering uses the ImageTrans project’s own layout; the rendering settings below do not apply. In-app rendering requests only text boxes and lays them out with the CSS and minimum font size below. If server rendering fails, the app falls back to text boxes.</string>
    <string name="settings_server_default_note">Uses the cloud server service.basiccat.org:51043 by default. To use ImageTrans on your computer, enter the computer’s LAN address, not local.basiccat.org (on a phone that resolves to the phone itself). If the LAN server uses a self-signed HTTPS certificate, install it as a trusted certificate in system settings first, or use an HTTP address.</string>
    <string name="settings_mymemory_section">MyMemory (Free)</string>
    <string name="settings_mymemory_email">Contact email (optional)</string>
    <string name="settings_mymemory_note">No API key is required. Each request can contain at most 500 bytes, so the app splits long paragraphs automatically. Leave this empty to use the built-in contact email (about 50,000 characters/day), or enter your own. The email is stored only on this device and sent with each request to MyMemory. As in the browser extension, "Auto" as the source is treated as Japanese and as the target as English.</string>
